{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel came</b> etc. In the fortieth year. It summarizes here what they traversed circling Mount Seir, from Kadesh Barnea to Kadesh in the wilderness of Zin, and it is included here all at once. These were the eighteen journeys written in the section of Maseot, from Rithmah to the wilderness of Zin. And concerning this it is said in the section of Devarim: ונפן ונסע המדבר דרך ים סוף ונסב את הר שעיר ימים רבים, etc., until: ונעבור מאת אחינו בני עשיו מאילת ומעציון גבר, and from there they came to Kadesh, which is in the land of Edom, as it is written in the section of Maseot: ויסעו מעציון גבר ויחנו במדבר צין היא קדש. What is missing here is the warning with which they were warned not to provoke the children of Esau, which is explained in the section of Devarim." "<b>And the people stayed in Kadesh.</b> They stayed there four months, until the month of Av, in which they came to Mount Hor, and there Aaron died. This is not the Kadesh about which it is said ותשבו בקדש ימים רבים, for that Kadesh is in the wilderness of Paran and is called Kadesh Barnea, and from it the spies were sent. But this Kadesh about which it is written <b>and the people stayed in Kadesh</b> is in the wilderness of Zin, on the border of the land of Edom." "<b>And Miriam died there.</b> Since it had already begun with the deaths of the wilderness, it appended to it the death of Miriam and Aaron."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:48.575290767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}